Author decision, 23 Oct 2026: use the span margin for the object task although the declared rule REJECTED it. It passed every validity check (single-word spans against score_words, 200 orders, 1.2e-4 bits; multi-word spans against an independent full-logits computation, 50 orders, 1.1e-4 bits; Spearman with the baseline margin 0.545; correct form preferred in 93.8% of orders) and failed only the rule that it reproduce the baseline intervening-subject contrast. mi_decompose_muril.md shows that contrast is not at the verb (agreeing words -0.23 bits, p 0.15) but in the scores of other words (-1.81 bits, p 1e-4), so the rule tested the wrong place. The contrast (attraction) task is dropped.
